The best interval we can use (the interval whose points are given that's closest to $x=-18$) is the interval between $x=-20$ and $x=-17$. Let's find the average rate of change between those points.

$\begin{align}
h'(-18)&\approx\dfrac{h(-17)-h(-20)}{-17-(-20)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{22-5}{3}
\\\\
&\approx5.67
\end{align}$
